# Sample machine-level Bazel config — see docs/CONFIGURATION.md § Shared Vendor
# Directory and § Remote Cache Configuration for background on each setting below.
#
# Copy this file to `~/.bazelrc` (your personal, machine-level Bazel config —
# NOT a file named `.bazelrc.user` inside the repo). Bazel automatically reads
# `~/.bazelrc` as its "home rc" on every invocation, regardless of which git
# worktree of this repo you're building from, so settings placed there are
# shared across every worktree on this machine without any per-worktree setup.
#
# Do not commit your personal `~/.bazelrc` — this file is only a template.
# Replace <you> below with your username (or the equivalent of $HOME).

# ── Vendor mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shares one copy of every external repo (bazel_dep's, Go modules, the Python
# interpreter/wheels, etc.) across every worktree on this machine, instead of
# each worktree's own output base independently fetching and extracting its
# own copy. Must be an absolute path outside any git worktree.
# Populate/refresh with `bazel vendor //...` after adding or updating a
# dependency (see the `vendor-sync` skill, which automates this).
common --vendor_dir=/home/<you>/.cache/bazel-vendor/everything

# ── Shared disk cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local action-result cache written outside any worktree, so builds and tests
# in one worktree reuse action outputs already produced by another worktree
# instead of recomputing them per-worktree output base.
build --disk_cache=/home/<you>/.cache/bazel-disk-cache/everything

# ── Remote cache (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Points at a shared remote cache so local builds can reuse action outputs
# produced by CI (and vice versa). See docs/CONFIGURATION.md § Remote Cache
# Configuration for the URL scheme (grpc(s):// or http(s)://) and auth options
# CI uses via the setup-build-env action. Uncomment and fill in to enable:
# build --remote_cache=grpcs://cache.example.com:443
# build --remote_cache_header=Authorization=Basic <base64-user:password>
# build --remote_upload_local_results=true
